    <div class="page">

        <div class="main-content">
            


<div class="content-page bg-primary ">
    <div class="heading-section color-overlay content-light " style="background-image: url('/-/media/Website/Images/ContentPageBanner.png');background-size:cover;">
        <div class="breadcrumb"></div>
                    <div class="container">
                <div class="row">
                    <div class="heading-content col-1 gold-bar"></div>
                </div>
                <div class="row">
                    <div class="heading-content col-12">
                        <h1>Blanket Orders &amp; Designation Orders</h1>

                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
    </div>

    <div class="content-section row content-dark bg-white">
            <div class="sidenav-container col-3">
                        <div class="sidebar-title title-small-border-blue">
            <div class="title">
                <a href="/en/securities-law-and-policy" class="">
                    <i class="gold-bar"></i>
                    Securities Law &amp; Policy
                </a>
            </div>
        </div>
    <div class="sidebar-nav-list">
            <ul>
                        <li class="child-title">
                            <a href="/en/securities-law-and-policy/act-and-regulation" class="">
                                <i class="gold-bar"></i>
                                Act &amp; Regulation
                            </a>


                        </li>
                        <li class="child-title">
                            <a href="/en/securities-law-and-policy/regulatory-instruments" class="">
                                <i class="gold-bar"></i>
                                Regulatory Instruments
                            </a>


                        </li>
                        <li class="child-title">
                            <a href="/en/securities-law-and-policy/regulatory-updates" class="">
                                <i class="gold-bar"></i>
                                Regulatory Updates
                            </a>


                        </li>
                        <li class="child-title">
                            <a href="/en/securities-law-and-policy/authorizations-and-memorandums-of-understanding" class="">
                                <i class="gold-bar"></i>
                                Authorizations &amp; Memorandums of Understanding
                            </a>


                        </li>
                        <li class="child-title">
                            <a href="/en/securities-law-and-policy/blanket-orders-and-designation-orders" class="active">
                                <i class="gold-bar"></i>
                                Blanket Orders &amp; Designation Orders
                            </a>


                        </li>
            </ul>
    </div>

            </div>

        <div class="container col-lg-9 col-sm-12 body-container color-overlay">
            <div class="row">
                <div class="col-12">
                    <div class="general-content">
                                                    <div class="body"><h1 class="page-title">Designation Orders</h1>
<p>Designation Orders are issued for the purpose of ensuring appropriate treatment of a particular matter that falls within Alberta securities laws. Most Designation Orders are made pursuant to section 10 of the <em>Securities Act</em> (Alberta), however, certain Rules also contemplate the issuance of Designation Orders. Current Designation Orders are listed below and can also be found, where relevant, in the <a href="/en/Securities-Law-and-Policy/Regulatory-Instruments">Regulatory Instruments</a>&nbsp;section of this website.</p>
<p>ASC Designation Orders currently in effect: </p>
<table class="table1 doc-table alt-table cell-border " style="width: 700px;">
    <tbody>
        <tr class="odd">
            <td style="width: 50px;"></td>
            <td style="width: 650px;"><a href="/-/media/ASC-Documents-part-2/Blanket-Orders-and-Designations/5320829-Designation-Order-re-45-108.pdf" target="_blank"><strong>Designation of a Crowdfunding Offering Document under Multilateral Instrument 45-108 <em>Crowdfunding as an Offering Memorandum</em></strong></a><strong><em><br />
            </em>
            <br />
            Status:</strong> Effective 31 October 2016</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="width: 50px;"></td>
            <td style="width: 650px;"><a href="/-/media/ASC-Documents-part-2/Blanket-Orders-and-Designations/Order-of-Designation-7-Certain-products-designated-to-be-securities-re-certain-orders-and-undertakin.pdf" target="_blank"><strong>Certain products designated to be securities re certain orders and undertaking s10(1)</strong></a> <strong><br />
            <br />
            Status:</strong> Effective 31 October 2014<strong> </strong></td>
        </tr>
        <tr class="odd">
            <td style="width: 50px;"></td>
            <td style="width: 650px;"><a href="/-/media/ASC-Documents-part-2/Blanket-Orders-and-Designations/4956337-v1-designation_order.pdf" target="_blank"><strong>Certain mortgage investment entities designated not to be non-redeemable investment funds (except for registration)</strong></a><strong><br />
            <br />
            Status:</strong> Effective 22 September 2014 </td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>
<h1 class="page-title">Blanket Orders</h1>
<p>Blanket Orders are issued for the purpose of providing mass exemptive relief (as opposed to providing an exemption for one individual or applicant) from a regulatory requirement. Current Blanket Orders are linked below and can also be found in the Regulatory Instruments section of this website. Blanket Orders that have expired or been revoked can also found in the Regulatory Instruments section, either on the history tab of the rule they affected, or on their own page. </p>
<p>ASC Blanket Orders currently in effect: </p>
<table class="table1 doc-table alt-table cell-border ">
    <tbody>
        <tr class="odd">
            <td style="width: 50px; vertical-align: middle;"><strong><a rel="noopener noreferrer" href="https://www.asc.ca/securities-law-and-policy/regulatory-instruments/23-930" target="_blank">23-930</a></strong></td>
            <td style="width: 650px;">
            <p><a href="/-/media/ASC-Documents-part-1/Regulatory-Instruments/2026/09/6304026-v1-Coordinated-Blanket-Order-23-930.pdf" target="_blank"><strong>Coordinated Blanket Order 23-930 <em>Temporary Exemption from Trading Fee Cap Requirements for Inter-listed Securities under National Instrument 23-101 Trading Rules</em></strong></a></p>
            <p>Status: Effective November 2 2026</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr class="odd">
            <td style="width: 50px; vertical-align: middle;"><strong><a rel="noopener noreferrer" href="https://www.asc.ca/securities-law-and-policy/regulatory-instruments/31-935" target="_blank">31-935</a></strong></td>
            <td style="width: 650px;">
            <p><strong><a href="/-/media/ASC-Documents-part-1/Regulatory-Instruments/2026/06/6270697-CSA-Notice--Coordinated-Blanket-Order-31-935.pdf" target="_blank">Coordinated Blanket Order 31-935 <em>Exemption from the Client Reporting Requirements for Certain Institutional Clients and Overflow Accounts of Registered Advisers</em></a></strong></p>
            <p>Status: Effective June 25 2026</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr class="odd">
            <td style="width: 50px; vertical-align: middle;"><strong><a rel="noopener noreferrer" href="https://www.asc.ca/securities-law-and-policy/regulatory-instruments/33-930" target="_blank">33-930</a></strong></td>
            <td style="width: 650px;">
            <p><a href="/-/media/ASC-Documents-part-1/Regulatory-Instruments/2026/04/6273002-Coordinated-Blanket-Order-33-930.pdf" target="_blank"><strong>Coordinated Blanket Order 33-930 <em>Exemptions from Requirements to Submit Certain Personal Information Under National Instrument 33-109 Registration Information</em></strong></a></p>
            <p>Status: Effective May 1 2026</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr class="odd">
